Subject: [PATCH] cmake: link libm on Linux

The Makefile build links libblasfeo.so with -lm, but the CMake build did
not, so the shared library had unresolved libm symbols (e.g. fminf) without
a DT_NEEDED entry and could not be loaded with dlopen(RTLD_NOW) unless libm
was already loaded.

---
--- a/CMakeLists.txt	2026-11-27 22:54:44
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt	2026-11-27 22:54:44
@@ -1417,6 +1417,12 @@
     VERSION ${BLASFEO_VERSION}
     SOVERSION ${BLASFEO_SOVERSION}
 )
+
+# BLASFEO uses math functions (e.g. fminf, sqrt), which live in a separate
+# libm on Linux; the Makefile build already links it with -lm.
+if(UNIX AND NOT APPLE)
+	target_link_libraries(blasfeo PRIVATE m)
+endif()
 
 # 1) *XILINX_NONE_ELF*:
